{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Why do the nations rage</b> — It seems correct to me that one of the poets composed this psalm concerning David on the day of his anointing; therefore it is written: \"I today have begotten you,\" or concerning the Messiah." "<b>And raged</b> — like חברו, and like it מרגשת פועלי און." "<b>The lamed of לאומים</b> — root, like ולאם מלאם יאמץ." "<b>Mutter vain things</b> — in speech, like ולשוני אם יהגה רמיה, and speech — their bonds are loosed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:04.481468877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}